  "description": "Deschutes: The Adventure Touring Bike with American Craftsmanship\nDiscover the Deschutes, a handmade adventure touring bike that combines Co-Motion’s renowned craftsmanship with unbeatable value. When we say value, we say compare it to nearly any bike you see in this on the rack of bikes made outside the US and you will see we are often a better price for a handmade in the USA, and made by a cyclist, not a machine. Built right here at Co-Motion HQ in Eugene, Oregon, this bike delivers the performance and quality of a true American-made bicycle, standing out among imported competitors. There are American companies, and then there are bikes made in America by cyclists just like you.\nKey Features:\n\nOptimized for 700c Wheels: Compatible with 30mm–50mm tires for stability and comfort on rugged terrain or smooth roads.\n\nDouble-Butted Cromoly Tubing: Hand-built for durability and a responsive ride feel.\n\nSteel Uni-Crown Touring Fork with 3 Pack Mount: Engineered for precise handling and support on loaded tours. Perfect for bikepacking.\n\nThru-Axles for Enhanced Stability: 142x12mm rear and 100x12mm front thru-axles keep you secure on any adventure.\n\nCo-Motion Touring Geometry: Proven geometry for comfort and control on long journeys.\n\nRack, Fender, and Bottle Mounts: Ready to be equipped to carry your gear, with three bottle mounts for extended hydration options.\n\nMechanical Disc Brakes and Hand-Built Wheels: Dependable braking power and rugged wheels built for the demands of adventure.\n\nWide-Range 2x11-Speed Shimano 105 Gearing: Smooth and reliable shifting for conquering climbs and cruising descents.\n\nColor for 2026: Sandy Sage\nChoose the Deschutes for its exceptional design, premium materials, and the pride of owning a handcrafted, American-made touring bike. Ready to go wherever your adventures take you!\n\nOffered as a complete bicycle only - $3,249\nSee features, pricing and options below",
